WEBVTT

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.950
Haruka! What is the meaning of this?

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:10.160
You suddenly went on extended leave?!
You never told me about this!

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:13.580
Haruka!

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.660
What... on Earth?

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.830
Haruka...

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.660
Just leave her be. Babying her
is just a waste of time.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.620
"A waste of..."?!

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.200
I swear! Do you honestly think hiding
in here is going to make things right?!

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.700
Yayoi...

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.120
Please give her some space for now.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.450
Underneath this sky, I have always

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.870
Continued to search for my dream

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.450
All alone...

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:23.080
Where does everyone go forth for their journey?

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:28.620
The days in my memories grow distant

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.370
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:40.120
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:50.450
I'm sure that with our silent profiles, both you and I

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.000
Understood that these personas exist

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.580
Because of our injuries

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:01.250
We say we do this for happiness or for love

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:05.700
As we repeat this cruel battle

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.330
Yet even so, the tears won't stop

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.750
Our hopeful hearts are one

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:20.500
Our own futures are calling to us

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:29.000
The Last Pudding

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.540
Hey, what have you been
working on this whole time?

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.410
Oh, right. They're New Year's cards.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.540
I hope you have a
happy New Year's.
Thank you for all
your help last year.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.540
You're writing New Year's cards now?
But tomorrow is New Year's Day.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.000
The past few days weren't really
the right time for this.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.370
Besides, I'm bored anyway.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.410
Yeah, we went through a lot, didn't we?

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.000
I never dreamed they'd completely remove
us from the Drop elimination rotations.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.500
It can't be helped, considering
the situation and all.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.910
Actually, it's creepy how we haven't
heard anything else from Headquarters.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.080
After what happened at Tsukimijima,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.500
I doubt we'll be receiving
more supplies for a while.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.040
Even Chikako grumbled about
how hard it is to make everything last.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.700
And here everyone was
so jovial up until Christmas...

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.290
Regardless, we cannot stay
down in the dumps.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:22.660
Let's make sure we are prepared to resume
work as soon as a mission comes in.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.870
Y-yes, sir!

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.160
By the way, where are
Mr. Saku and Miss Azusa?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.000
Sir, Saku left to report to our
headquarters in Geneva.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:32.790
And Azusa is...

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.160
And Azusa is...
Right, this is the Operations Command Room.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:34.790
Where did she go...?
Right, this is the Operations Command Room.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:35.700
Where did she go...?
Right.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:36.830
Director!

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.700
There is a call for you from an outside line.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.040
Who could it be?

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.750
Well, all he said was that
you were friends in college.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.080
Put him on the line.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.000
Yes, sir!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.330
Hello.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.910
My, this takes me back!

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.620
How have you been?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.200
I see, I see.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.200
Hey! Are you taking that to your master?

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:14.200
Yes...

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:19.290
I got my hands on some delicious tea, so
I was thinking we could enjoy it together.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.250
Why don't you give it a rest?
Just watching you pisses me off.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.830
Right now, I am very happy.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.120
How about you?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.080
Me...?

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:55.540
At last... You've finally
come back, my Imber.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.790
This will open the path to
humanity's... to YOUR future.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.910
My future?

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.830
That was the very first time Imber and I met.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.830
What's with those kids?

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.790
They're adopted. The professors must
be getting pretty anxious, huh?

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:20.830
Well, they'll be in trouble if they don't
show some results and fast.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.000
This department eats through money.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:28.500
Wait a sec. Does this mean those
kids are test subjects?

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:38.790
This is incredible!

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:39.830
Success is just in sight!

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.870
We can move our research
on to the next level.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:59.540
I wanted to become one with Imber...
To be with him forever.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.540
So when I heard of their plan, I was happy.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.910
The Mischling Plan?!
Is Professor Teru Lo-Wu serious?

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.790
Yeah. Supposedly Headquarters
has given the approval.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:15.700
Wasn't that the plan for fusing
an iDOL and a human?

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.580
So are those girls the test subjects?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.830
Yeah. Supposedly the guinea pig
sisters volunteered.

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:22.500
They're all crazy!

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.950
In the end, they were only able
to become Bastards.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.580
Do you think you will get away
with doing this to me?

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.910
I see you can still speak.

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:43.660
And here we haven't so much as
given you water in five days...

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.750
Naturally. It's because I'm a-

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.330
Mischling, the complete fusion
of the alien creature

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.620
known as an iDOL and a human being.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:55.160
But in all actuality,
such a creature does not exist.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.700
It's merely an illusion.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:01.830
That isn't true! I am a Mischling.
I can adapt to any environment.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.040
I am a new form of human.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.040
That must be what that woman taught you.

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.330
And yet you seem to be suffering.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:12.160
Shut up! Don't call Mama "that woman"!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.660
Mama's wishes are my desires!

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:21.540
Father, your wishes are my desires.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.910
Back then, when I trembled with fear...

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.080
I'm sure that ever since then...

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.040
Hey, did you hear?
Those two are having at it again.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.910
They're in opposition over
the Mischling Plan, huh?

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.120
Professor Cayenne just can't
make up his mind, can he?

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:56.250
Well, it's just a matter of time before
Professor Teru goes over his head.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.750
Epimetheus?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.250
Right. We turn a human's mind into data
and plant it inside the iDOL

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.830
in an attempt to fuse humans and iDOLs.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.160
It's part of the Mischling Plan.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.910
You would go that far...

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.000
There is no need for concern.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.660
We will give birth to a Mischling
before things come to that.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:28.290
Once it's born, I won't have to put you
through all of this hardship anymore...

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:29.950
Father...

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:37.910
That's right.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.410
I offered my body because it
was what he wanted.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.540
But...

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.410
Large explosions in Hangars 4 and 5. Fire in No. 6.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.120
The medical clinic is full!
Have the injured sleep in the halls!
Large explosions in Hangars 4 and 5. Fire in No. 6.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:52.910
The medical clinic is full!
Have the injured sleep in the halls!
Firefighter platoons are ordered
to Level A scramble!

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.450
Area F, Section A: Someone respond!
Firefighter platoons are ordered
to Level A scramble!

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.330
There's no point calling them.
That area has already been blocked off.

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.410
There is a poisonous gas leak in the
biochemistry lab on Level 8, Block A!

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.500
Yurakucho has been turned into a sea of fire!
Prepare to close the emergency partitions!

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:05.660
Section Leader, please respond! Section Leader!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.910
Why?!

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.370
Why are you doing this?!
I did this all for you!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.700
I sacrificed everything just for you!

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.040
Imber...

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.910
In Memory
of Those Lost
in the
Dawn of the
Purple Moon

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.250
Dawn of the Purple Moon...

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.750
It's the day we cut our ties with Mondenkind
and began to call ourselves Turiavita.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.750
It's the day I was torn away from you...

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:39.160
But now I can feel you forever.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:43.500
I can feel you... up close like this.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.040
Imber...

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.790
I see that your meeting is over, Saku.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.750
Thanks to you it went without a hitch.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:40.410
I also successfully tweaked things
with the various nations.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:42.410
Please pull some strings
for the remaining parties.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:44.790
I have already taken care of that.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.790
How does it feel?

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:51.040
It's been some time since you sat
as Chief Commander of MSA.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.580
Well, it sure is a pain in the neck.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.410
A youngster like me is best fit
for working on the field.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.330
We expect much from you, Saku.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.080
Right.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:03.950
Time left until New Year's Day:
Local Forecast: Tokyo-Sunny,
Kanagawa Prefecture-Sunny...

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.830
Time left until New Year's Day:
7 Hours 35 Minutes...
Local Forecast: Tokyo-Sunny,
Kanagawa Prefecture-Sunny...

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.250
Keep
our city
clean.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.250
You're early, just like always.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.910
I believe in doing everything perfectly.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.910
That's just like you.

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:36.580
You shouldn't delve too deeply.
Cats have surprisingly sharp claws.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:38.830
Now, then...

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:44.830
I'm pretty sure this is how they
say it in Japan. "Have a nice year."

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:52.830
I see...

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.450
Is he a "cat"?

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.830
All systems: Green.
Launch Sequence: In progress.

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:01.620
I've confirmed that all lines
have been disconnected.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.080
Put Imber in the pit.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:03.500
The launch pit's canal is clear.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.000
Why aren't you using me?
The launch pit's canal is clear.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:06.160
You may put Imber inside.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.660
If you sent Hiems and I...

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.870
If you sent me...

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:21.790
So we're doing this impromtu?

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:26.450
It'll be okay. Knowing Iori,
she'll pull through for us somehow.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:28.660
We're counting on you!

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.790
Got it!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.410
Hey, attention please!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.580
I'm taking orders for anyone who wants
New Year's Soba Noodles!

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:40.160
Delivery? Then I'll have some
tempura soba noodles.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:41.200
Same here!

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.500
I'd like tempura on rice!

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.040
These are supposed
to be New Year's noodles.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:47.080
Are we getting this from Choju-an?
They take forever to deliver.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:47.870
What?!

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:58.790
Jeez. "It's a Master's job to rest
when she can," my butt!

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.830
I can't believe Ritsuko.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.580
Tempura
Soba Noodles

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.660
I'm going to eat now!

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:34.950
Tempura

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:34.580
This is a must on New Year's Eve!
Oh, yeah! Drinks, drinks...

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.200
Let's see... Lucky!

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:44.500
I might be lucky clear
to the end of the year!

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:50.200
HARUKA'S
PUDDING

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:51.870
Iori, you can't have that yet!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.160
Why not?

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:55.700
We're going to eat this
together after dinner!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.500
It doesn't matter when we eat them.

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:02.790
This is mine! It's the new
strawberry milk flavor!

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:05.250
What? Strawberry milk?

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:07.910
Yep! Doesn't it look good?

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.160
Oh, Yukiho! Do you have a pen?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:12.160
Sure do!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.410
Let's see...

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.160
HARUKA'S
PUDDING

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:17.660
This belongs to me now,
so don't go eating it.

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:19.250
Yukiho, you should-

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.370
Yukiho, not again!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.330
I wasn't asleep.

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.120
What?!

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.450
Honest, I wasn't!

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:28.160
HARUKA'S
PUDDING

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:36.080
Wow, there's some pudding!
What ever should I do?

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.660
Should I go ahead and eat it?

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.120
It's going to expire...

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.620
Can you move your fingers?

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:52.080
Yup, they're okay. This is part of the,
uh... rehabilitation, right?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:05.160
The Cat's Grand Lodge...

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:11.250
It would appear that
we are mice kept by cats.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:16.580
Miss Azusa, did you know...?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:20.790
I'm sorry. Please give me a little more time.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:23.290
Once everything is over...

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:33.330
It's been a while since we
played together last, hasn't it?

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:37.120
Do you think Tempestas is listening?

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.450
Yes.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.790
Happy
New
Year.

00:17:50.700 --> 00:17:51.660
That hurt!

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:55.160
This is good!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.580
Hi! I'm Yayoi Takatsuki!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:32.700
Man, it's festive out here! Isn't this
amazing? There's so very many people!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.790
Night shall soon break.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.660
This will bring a new dawn for humanity.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:12.660
Our Turiavita will lead
the people to a new world.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:22.910
What?! Got it. I'm on my way.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:40.500
It took place on an uninhabited island
with a 200 meter circumference,

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:44.660
but we expect the missing landmass to have
a large effect on the nearby ocean waters.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.040
What a nasty way to start the New Year, huh?

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:51.790
Indeed. And here we're supposed to have
Mondenkind to prevent this from happening...

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:51.790
Live Footage from Where the Drop Landed

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.080
I believe that it is now time to reassess
the way Mondenkind functions.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:56.080
What... is this?
I believe that it is now time to reassess
the way Mondenkind functions.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:56.750
I believe that it is now time to reassess
the way Mondenkind functions.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:57.290
My heart is racing.
I believe that it is now time to reassess
the way Mondenkind functions.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:59.120
My heart is racing.
You have a point.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:02.080
Well then, to change the topic,
we have information on a New Year's event.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.080
Hey, what is this all about?!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.370
I heard an iDOL was behind that accident.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.500
Well...

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.450
"To everyone in Mondenkind,"

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:16.160
"We would like you to hand over
all of the iDOLs in your possession

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:18.910
"to our company, Turiavita,
in all due haste."

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.080
"If you refuse to meet our demands,

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.660
"we will be left with no choice
but to continue our assault."

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:32.200
"I hope and pray that you swallow our
demands before any civilians are harmed."

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:38.410
What the hell? Wasn't that a declaration
of war? The cocky jerks...!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.790
Ma'am, let me launch Nebula!

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:43.410
Where would you go when we don't
know what their next target is?

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:45.660
But at this rate...!

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:51.500
Everyone, did you hear what
Turiavita's demands are?

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:57.160
The situation has become dire,
but, hey, there is no need for concern.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:01.620
Here's your notice from
Mondenkind's HQ in Geneva.

00:21:02.450 --> 00:21:09.700
"As of today, January 1st, Mondenkind
Japan's iDOL Team has been disbanded."

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.910
What is this? Why is my heart racing?
Could it be...?

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.500
Amazing!

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:47.450
It's an iDOL! Bye-bye, iDOL!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.500
Oh, yeah. Did you watch the news today?
There was a segment on a meteorite.
It's an iDOL! Bye-bye, iDOL!

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.870
Imber...

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:05.250
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:14.250
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:23.120
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:31.660
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:43.080
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:52.080
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:52.080 --> 00:23:01.000
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:12.620
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:41.000
Preview
Key and Bat

00:23:26.950 --> 00:23:29.000
Yayoi, we got a postcard!

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:33.040
Let's see. It says, "Please come up
with an afternoon version of 'ya-yoi-yo.'"

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:36.450
Huh? "It's a good Yafternoon"?
Too lame! Crap!

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.160
"Yah, yo! Morning!" That's no good.

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.450
Uh, Ya-yoo!

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:40.790
We're accepting suggestions!
